                <pb facs="0257" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1888</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-08T13:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In view of the fact that the currency loan option expires April 18, the
                    representatives of the British, French, Japanese, and Russian groups have asked
                    the Chinese Government for an extension. The Russian and Japanese groups are
                    therefore now treated as direct parties in interest in matters concerning the
                    currency loan. How far has the formation of an American group proceeded?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
